# Frag Arena / Degen Tournament — server configuration.
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in. Everything here is OPTIONAL: with an empty file
# the game runs exactly as it does today, with the external feeds off and the wallet read
# on the free public RPC. The shell always wins over this file, so
#   PUMP_CA=<other> npm run server
# points one run at a different coin without editing anything.
#
# server/env.js loads this. It must stay the FIRST import in serverMain.js — several
# modules capture their config into consts at import time, and a var that arrives after
# that is a var that silently does nothing.

# ── SOLANA ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which RPC the read-only wallet link uses to see what a player holds.
#
# WHY YOU WANT A PAID ONE: the grant is derived from a getProgramAccounts scan over
# mpl-core, and on the free public RPC that measured ~26 SECONDS on mainnet. It works —
# the grant is applied to a live body whenever it lands — but the player spends most of a
# minute holding a pistol they did not pay for. A Helius endpoint turns that into a normal
# request. Drop the key in and this is the only line that changes.
# SOLANA_RPC=https://mainnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=YOUR_KEY_HERE

# Abort the wallet read after this long. 45s is sized for the slow public RPC; with a paid
# endpoint you can cut it hard, and a low value here is a good way to notice a bad one.
# WALLET_RPC_TIMEOUT_MS=45000

# The Season 1 collection. Defaults to mainnet (common/entitlements.js). Override BOTH
# this and SOLANA_RPC together to point a dev server at devnet — they must agree, or a
# holder is read against the wrong chain, finds nothing, and spawns with a pistol.
# DEGEN_COLLECTION=CS9gJkpP9CUY834gYC19aWmtZSGAw2Rchj1aoMBG1NNC

# ── PUMP.FUN LIVECHAT -> ARENA CHAT ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The coin's contract address. This is the ONE value that switches the pump.fun feed on:
# with it set, server/chatBridge.js joins that coin's livechat room and pipes messages
# into the arena chat log tagged PUMP. Without it the bridge logs that it is off and does
# nothing else.
#
# READ-ONLY, one directional, by design. Nothing in the game relays back OUT to pump.fun —
# that would need a credential on a path a player can reach, and the rule inherited from
# the Tokidoki rig is that anything able to move money or spend a key lives in the private
# half, never here.
#
# Needs socket.io-client installed (pump.fun livechat is socket.io); the bridge degrades
# to off with a log line rather than crashing if it is missing.
# PUMP_CA=
# PUMP_LIVECHAT=https://livechat.pump.fun

# ── TELEGRAM -> ARENA CHAT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Same one-way bridge, from a Telegram group. Bot token from @BotFather.
# TELEGRAM_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ── PROOF OF BLOOD ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Block length. Production is 10 minutes (600000) and should stay there — this exists so a
# test can close blocks in seconds instead of waiting out a real window.
# BLOOD_BLOCK_MS=600000

# ── ARENA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MAP pins one map and PAUSES rotation; MODE forces TDM/FFA. Both are dev/probe switches.
# MAP=
# MODE=
# ROTATE=1
# MAPINFO_PORT=8078
